WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:05.360
As we head towards an epic face-off between
the Avengers and Thanos in Avengers: Infinity

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:09.490
War, it's crucial to keep track of what's
going on with the Infinity Stones, and Doctor

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:13.360
Strange's solo movie reveals an important
new piece in the infinity stone puzzle!

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:17.500
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and I'm
going to talk about a cool infinity stone

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:22.189
reveal from Doctor Strange and give you a
full update on the status of all six Infinity

00:00:22.189 --> 00:00:23.980
Stones in the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:28.070
Just so you're aware there will be spoilers
coming up for Doctor Strange, so if you haven't

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:32.529
seen the movie yet or want to avoid those,
click here for my spoiler-free movie review.

00:00:32.529 --> 00:00:37.649
OK, let's first recap the key updates we get
in Doctor Strange about the Infinity Stones.

00:00:37.649 --> 00:00:41.640
The movie reveals that the Eye of Agamotto
holds an infinity stone, the Time Stone in

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:42.640
fact.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:46.530
As its name suggests, the Time Stone has the
power to manipulate the space-time continuum

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:50.989
and we first see this after Strange uses the
Eye of Agamotto to cast a spell where he moves

00:00:50.989 --> 00:00:56.100
an apple backwards and forwards in time, from
whole to eaten and decayed and back to whole

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.100
again.

00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:00.829
Strange even uses it to restore the stolen
pages from the Book of Cagliostro and there's

00:01:00.829 --> 00:01:05.360
that sudden moment where columns of glass
or crystal shoot up in front of him, disappearing

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:09.720
as Wong and Mordo burst in and scold him for
the dangers of manipulating the space-time

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:10.720
continuum.

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:14.659
So, there's an interesting bit of foreshadowing
in this scene, with Mordo warning Strange

00:01:14.659 --> 00:01:18.500
about getting stuck in a time loop, which
of course is the trick that Strange uses later

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:19.640
against Dormammu.

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:24.470
And the mirrored images that pop up suggest
Strange is peeking into visions of alternate

00:01:24.470 --> 00:01:25.470
timelines.

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:30.119
By the way, even when time spells aren't being
cast, the movie plays on the theme of time

00:01:30.119 --> 00:01:34.340
with lingering shots of Strange's collection
of expensive watches and with Strange asking

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:37.030
Dr West to cover his watch during an operation.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:41.909
Later in the movie, Doctor Strange again opens
the Eye of Agamotto in Hong Kong, using the

00:01:41.909 --> 00:01:46.329
time Stone to roll back significant events
in time, restoring demolished buildings and

00:01:46.329 --> 00:01:48.360
even bringing Wong back to life.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:52.440
And during his confrontation with Dormammu,
Strange also cheats death himself with the

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:53.920
creation of a time loop.

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:58.659
These scenes were visually very cool and impressive,
but the resurrection that the Time Stone seems

00:01:58.659 --> 00:02:01.640
to allow has wider implications for the MCU.

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:05.240
For example, could it bring back a fallen
Avenger like Quicksilver?

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:08.200
Obviously, there are risks to using the Time
Stone.

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:13.080
Mordo is opposed to using it in the film as
it's against natural law, and his words "the

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:17.600
bill comes due" could be foreshadowing Thanos
getting hold of the Time Stone.

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:22.070
As Wong said, news of the Ancient One's death
will spread rapidly through the multiverse

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:26.110
and Thanos may also have detected Strange
using the stone in the Dark Dimension as we

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:28.770
know he's tracking where all the stones are.

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:32.910
By the way, talking of Mordo, going forward
keep a look-out for the Staff of the Living

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:37.250
Tribunal which Mordo mentioned when explaining
magical relics to Doctor Strange.

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:41.520
The Living Tribunal is a character in the
Marvel comic book multiverse with power that

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:46.350
eclipses even that of the Infinity Gauntlet,
and the way Mordo gave a special mention to

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:50.370
the Staff of the Living Tribunal could mean
we'll see this relic or the character come

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.180
into play in Infinity War.

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:56.421
So, now we've seen the Time Stone in action,
Wong and Strange have decided to leave the

00:02:56.421 --> 00:03:00.870
Eye of Agamotto alone in a room that was already
broken into by Kaecilius and his Zealots.

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:05.640
If it stays there, it's not hard to imagine
how Thanos will get his hands on it!

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:07.260
And what about the other five stones?

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:13.010
Well, we've got four others accounted for
so far: the Space Stone, the Reality Stone,

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:15.500
the Power Stone, and the Mind Stone.

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:20.640
The Space stone, also known as the Tesseract,
can act as an energy source and also open

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:24.340
up portals in space to allow teleportation
between worlds.

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:28.510
It was harnessed by Red Skull in the first
Captain America movie, stolen from SHIELD

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:33.220
by Loki in The Avengers, and last seen being
taken back to Asgard by Thor at the end of

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:36.000
that movie and stored in Odin's Treasure Room.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:40.500
But with Loki masquerading as Odin at the
end of Thor: The Dark World, could the stone

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:43.130
have already fallen into the wrong hands?

00:03:43.130 --> 00:03:48.790
The Reality stone, aka the Aether, is extremely
powerful and was wielded by Malekith in Thor:

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:49.840
The Dark World.

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:54.710
The Aether takes on a liquid form rather than
a solid state, and Odin has said it can convert

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:56.450
matter into dark matter.

00:03:56.450 --> 00:04:00.690
It's not completely clear yet what else it
can do, but it is extremely dangerous as it

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:03.840
reputedly has the power to destroy the whole
Universe.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:08.180
Ironically, given he seems a pretty shady
character, it was handed over for safekeeping

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:13.200
to Taneleer Tivan, aka the Collector, at the
end of The Dark World, although events later

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:17.480
in Guardians of the Galaxy led to an explosion
at Tivan's collection, so it's unknown whether

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:19.450
the Aether is still in his possession.

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:24.480
And it was the Guardians of the Galaxy who
introduced the Power Stone, which Thanos had

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:26.850
ordered Ronan the Accuser to obtain for him.

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:30.880
The Power Stone, as its name suggests, is
incredibly powerful and can even destroy a

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:33.380
whole planet if it falls into the wrong hands.

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:37.150
It was handed over to the Nova Corps at the
end of Guardians of the Galaxy who put it

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:39.480
in their vault for supposed safekeeping.

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:43.870
In the comics, the Nova Corps derive much
of their power from the Nova Force which could

00:04:43.870 --> 00:04:48.150
suggest the Nova Corps might try to harness
the energy from the Power Stone.

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:53.090
The Mind Stone has featured in both Avengers
movies so far, first brought to Earth by Loki

00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:56.260
in his sceptre and used to mind-control Hawkeye.

00:04:56.260 --> 00:05:00.720
After it fell into the hands of HYDRA, it
was used to harness the latent powers of Scarlet

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:05.350
Witch and Quicksilver, and later when Tony
Stark recovered it, it was one of the elements

00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:07.100
used to bring Vision to life.

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:10.420
And the Mind Stone is currently embedded in
Vision's forehead.

00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:15.590
The stone we haven't yet seen, the Soul Stone,
will presumably show up in one of the films

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:18.810
before Avengers: Infinity War or in Infinity
War itself.

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:23.850
In the comics, the Soul Stone is sentient,
hungers for other souls and it has the power

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:28.860
over life and death, all of which mean it's
a good candidate for turning up in Thor: Ragnarok

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:32.670
which will introduce Cate Blanchett as the
supernatural villain Hela.

00:05:32.670 --> 00:05:37.950
Hela is an Asgardian goddess, Queen of Hel
and has a history of stealing souls in the

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:42.470
comics, which could mean she either already
has the stone or knows where it is and is

00:05:42.470 --> 00:05:43.470
going to steal it.

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:47.780
There was a scene from Hel teased in Thor's
vision in Avengers: Age of Ultron and Thor

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:52.170
also had a vision of the Infinity Stones which
he decided to investigate at the end of that

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:56.850
Avengers movie, all of which points to an
important infinity stone reveal in Thor: Ragnarok.

00:05:56.850 --> 00:06:02.420
By the way, there's also a theory that Heimdall
possesses the Soul Stone, indicated by his

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:06.610
glowing orange eyes, and that the Stone can
be seen in his armour.

00:06:06.610 --> 00:06:11.980
So guys, we now have the location of the Time
Stone in the MCU confirmed, but we're still

00:06:11.980 --> 00:06:13.380
missing the Soul Stone.

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:15.860
What movie do you think it's going to show
up in?

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:20.270
And what are your predictions for how Thanos
is going to get hold of all six stones?

